{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a7e3c1d2-9b44-4f10-8c6e-2d5a1f0b3c88",
    "name": "OpenRegister Register Descriptors API",
    "description": "The register-descriptor inventory and the forced re-import.\n\nWHY THESE ARE CONTRACT TESTS\n\nEighteen fleet apps ship a register descriptor and import it from a Repair step. Repair steps run on install and `occ upgrade`, and `occ upgrade` reports \"No upgrade required\" once an app's version settles — so the import can never run again. The steps are documented never to throw: a failure logs a warning and leaves the instance looking healthy.\n\nThe consequence was measured, not imagined: an `occ upgrade` that reported complete success left 8 of 15 declared registers absent, including `flows`, and two e2e suites died on the missing register.\n\nSo the assertions here are mostly about what the API says when something is WRONG. A contract suite that only exercises the healthy row would reproduce the silence this endpoint exists to break.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "GET /api/register-descriptors → every declared register, with a state",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "OCS-APIRequest",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/index.php/apps/openregister/api/register-descriptors",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "index.php",
            "apps",
            "openregister",
            "api",
            "register-descriptors"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the inventory answers 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('it carries rows and the three counts', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('results');",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('total');",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('absent');",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('behind');",
              "});",
              "",
              "// 🔴 THE ABSENT COUNT IS A FIRST-CLASS FIELD, not something a client has to",
              "// derive by filtering. A consumer that has to compute 'is anything wrong'",
              "// is one that will render a healthy-looking total and move on — which is",
              "// the exact failure this endpoint was built to end.",
              "pm.test('absent and behind are reported as counts, not left to the client', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.absent).to.be.a('number');",
              "  pm.expect(body.behind).to.be.a('number');",
              "});",
              "",
              "const rows = body.results || [];",
              "pm.test('every row names its app, slug, state and shipped version', () => {",
              "  rows.forEach((r) => {",
              "    pm.expect(r).to.have.property('appId');",
              "    pm.expect(r).to.have.property('slug');",
              "    pm.expect(['current', 'behind', 'absent']).to.include(r.state);",
              "    pm.expect(r.shippedVersion, r.slug + ' ships a version').to.be.a('string');",
              "  });",
              "});",
              "",
              "// absent and present are told apart by installedVersion being NULL, not by",
              "// a truthy check on a string. `behind` and `absent` both 'need attention'",
              "// and need different actions, so nothing may collapse them.",
              "pm.test('an absent row has no installed version, a present one does', () => {",
              "  rows.forEach((r) => {",
              "    if (r.state === 'absent') { pm.expect(r.installedVersion, r.slug).to.be.null; }",
              "    else { pm.expect(r.installedVersion, r.slug).to.not.be.null; }",
              "  });",
              "});",
              "",
              "const current = rows.find((r) => r.state === 'current');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('descApp', current ? current.appId : '');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('descSlug', current ? current.slug : '');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "POST re-import a register whose version already matches → still writes",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "OCS-APIRequest",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/index.php/apps/openregister/api/register-descriptors/{{descApp}}/{{descSlug}}/import",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "index.php",
            "apps",
            "openregister",
            "api",
            "register-descriptors",
            "{{descApp}}",
            "{{descSlug}}",
            "import"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Skipped only when this instance holds no current register at all — and",
              "// the skip says so, rather than passing quietly over an untested path.",
              "if (!pm.collectionVariables.get('descSlug')) {",
              "  pm.test.skip('SKIPPED — no register on this instance is present and current, so the version-gate case is UNVERIFIED by this run');",
              "} else {",
              "  pm.test('the forced re-import answers 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "  const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "  // 🔴 THE WHOLE POINT. ImportHandler short-circuits on",
              "  // `version_compare(shipped, installed, '<=')` unless forced, and the",
              "  // versions match in exactly the case an administrator presses this. An",
              "  // unforced import would report success having written nothing.",
              "  pm.test('a version-matched re-import reports imported, never skipped', () => {",
              "    pm.expect(body.outcome).to.eql('imported');",
              "  });",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "POST re-import a register the app does not declare → 422 naming the slug",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "OCS-APIRequest",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/index.php/apps/openregister/api/register-descriptors/openregister/no-such-register-9f3a1c/import",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "index.php",
            "apps",
            "openregister",
            "api",
            "register-descriptors",
            "openregister",
            "no-such-register-9f3a1c",
            "import"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('an undeclared register is refused with 422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('the outcome is failed', () => pm.expect(body.outcome).to.eql('failed'));",
              "",
              "// The reason must NAME the slug. 'Import failed' leaves an administrator",
              "// unable to tell a typo from a broken descriptor from a missing app — three",
              "// different next steps.",
              "pm.test('the reason names the slug that could not be found', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(String(body.reason)).to.include('no-such-register-9f3a1c');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "POST re-import for an app that ships nothing → refused, and says why",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "OCS-APIRequest",
            "value": "true"
          },
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/index.php/apps/openregister/api/register-descriptors/no-such-app-7c2b/flows/import",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "index.php",
            "apps",
            "openregister",
            "api",
            "register-descriptors",
            "no-such-app-7c2b",
            "flows",
            "import"
          ]
        },
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{}"
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('an unknown app is refused with 422', () => pm.response.to.have.status(422));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('and the refusal is reported, not swallowed', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.outcome).to.eql('failed');",
              "  pm.expect(body.reason, 'a reported failure carries its reason').to.be.a('string');",
              "  pm.expect(body.reason).to.not.eql('');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
